    "description": {
      "en": "Marks the €500,000 income threshold that plays a double role in the CEHR schedule computed by tin_fr's SchedCalc: it is the upper edge of the first CEHR band for singles and the first band edge for couples (\"Exceptional contributions on high income earners: singles\"). The same value is reused as the Elig_Cond eligibility threshold for couples in tinto01_fr's screening for the Contribution Différentielle sur les Hauts Revenus (CDHR), consistent with the country report's statement that CDHR concerns couples with reference income above €500,000."
